content:
Looking at the folds: the first fold along the horizontal line reflects the strip so the two legs make angles of 70° with the horizontal. The second fold along the line of one leg reflects the other leg, sending it to a direction making 30° below the horizontal (since 2·70° − 290° = −150°, i.e., 210°). The third fold mirrors this flap across the vertical, giving flaps at 210° and 330°. The angle β between the two flaps (measured below the center) is 330° − 210° = 120°.

Checking: β = 120° is consistent with α = 70° through the sequence of reflections.

\boxed{C}
